n:Lax117284.Theorem7.reduce_polyTime:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"Theorem7.reduce_polyTime","nodeId":"c:Lax117284.Theorem7","semanticId":"Lax117284.Theorem7.reduce_polyTime"},"dock:Lax117284.Theorem7.uniform_three_one_npHard":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284.Theorem7.html#s-Lax117284.Theorem7.uniform_three_one_npHard","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.uniform_three_one_npHard:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"Theorem7.uniform_three_one_npHard","nodeId":"c:Lax117284.Theorem7","semanticId":"Lax117284.Theorem7.uniform_three_one_npHard"},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.correct:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.inst_days:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.inst_p_eq:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.reduce_polyTime:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax429075.EncodingCorrect:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax429075.SATHard:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:assumption:Lax759944.TuringRamPolytimeEquivalence:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.uniform_three_one_npHard:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Hardness.uniform_three_one_npHard"},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Machine.SatFinal.reduce_polyTime":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Machine.SatFinal.reduce_polyTime.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Machine.SatFinal.reduce_polyTime:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.reduce_polyTime:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The reduction is a word RAM program on the zeros and ones of its input: a one-pass tokenizer reads\nthe formula — the number of variables, the numbers of clauses of two and of three literals, and a\nvariable and a sign for every position —, a first pass checks, for every position, that its\nvariable is one of the formula's and that its literal has not occurred twice before it, which is a\nloop over the earlier positions that counts, and a second pass writes the image, the due date of\nevery client on each of the three days being a case analysis on the number of the client that\ncounts, on the third day, the earlier positions with the same literal. The number of variables is\nrequired not to exceed the number of positions, which keeps the image polynomial in the input. A\nword that is not the code of such a formula is answered with the rejected word. The numbers may be\nexponential in the length of the input, which the word length of a polynomial-time word RAM\naccommodates, and polynomial time on the word RAM transfers to a Turing machine.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Machine.SatFinal.reduce_polyTime","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Machine.SatFinal.reduce_polyTime","tooltipHtml":"The reduction is a word RAM program on the zeros and ones of its input: a one-pass tokenizer reads\nthe formula — the number of variables, the numbers of clauses of two and of three literals, and a\nvariable and a sign for every position —, a first pass checks, for every position, that its\nvariable is one of the formula's and that its literal has not occurred twice before it, which is a\nloop over the earlier positions that counts, and a second pass writes the image, the due date of\nevery client on each of the three days being a case analysis on the number of the client that\ncounts, on the third day, the earlier positions with the same literal. The number of variables is\nrequired not to exceed the number of positions, which keeps the image polynomial in the input. A\nword that is not the code of such a formula is answered with the rejected word. The numbers may be\nexponential in the length of the input, which the word length of a polynomial-time word RAM\naccommodates, and polynomial time on the word RAM transfers to a Turing machine."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_days":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_days.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_days:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.inst_days:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The construction names three days.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_days","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_days","tooltipHtml":"The construction names three days."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_p_eq":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_p_eq.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_p_eq:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.inst_p_eq:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Every processing time of the construction is `2`.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_p_eq","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Structural.inst_p_eq","tooltipHtml":"Every processing time of the construction is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span>."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.Theorem7.correct":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.Theorem7.correct.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.Theorem7.correct:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.correct:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The three dummies conflict with each other on all three days, so exactly one of them runs\non each day; the first day then admits one client of every group, which is the assignment\nand one client of every clause, the second day is a dead end for everything but a client of\na clause of three literals, and on the third day a client of an occurrence conflicts with\nexactly the variable client that falsifies its literal.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.Theorem7.correct","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.Theorem7.correct","tooltipHtml":"The three dummies conflict with each other on all three days, so exactly one of them runs\non each day; the first day then admits one client of every group, which is the assignment\nand one client of every clause, the second day is a dead end for everything but a client of\na clause of three literals, and on the third day a client of an occurrence conflicts with\nexactly the variable client that falsifies its literal."},"p:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct":{"href":"../lax-117284/Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct.html","incident":["e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.correct:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.inst_days:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct:assumption:Lax117284.Theorem7.inst_p_eq:0","e:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct:conclusion:Lax117284.Theorem7.reduce_correct:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"A word encoding a formula is sent to the code of the constructed instance, which has three days and equal processing times, and the code determines the instance; every other word goes to the rejected word.","nodeId":"p:Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct","semanticId":"Lax117284Proofs.WordCorrect.theorem7_reduce_correct","tooltipHtml":"A word encoding a formula is sent to the code of the constructed instance, which has three days and equal processing times, and the code determines the instance; every other word goes to the rejected word."}}},"status":"6 statements; 6 proofs","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"prepared-graph\" width=\"986\" height=\"492\" viewBox=\"0 0 986 492\" aria-label=\"Proof dependency graph\" data-layout-digest=\"ea094ae4ab